<title>USA: IMC-Agrico buys phosphate reserves for $31 mln.</title>
<headline>IMC-Agrico buys phosphate reserves for $31 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>IMC-Agrico Co, a joint venture of IMC Global Inc and Freeport-McMoRan Resource Partners LP, said Monday it has bought about 24,000 acres of phosphate-bearing land in central Florida for about $31 million and future royalties.</p>
<p>The land contains more than 100 million tons of high-quality recoverable phosphate rock, IMC-Agrico said.</p>
<p>The acquisition increases IMC-Agrico's rock reserves by more than 25 percent, the partnership said.</p>
<p>IMC-Agrico produces phosphate rock, concentrated phosphate crop nutrients and animal feed ingredients.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
